e":"Scott Morrison","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10468","person_slug":"scott-morrison","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sharon Bird","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10043","person_slug":"sharon-bird","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sharon Grierson","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10266","person_slug":"sharon-grierson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Shayne Neumann","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10485","person_slug":"shayne-neumann","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sid Sidebottom","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10583","person_slug":"sid-sidebottom","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Simon Crean","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10158","person_slug":"simon-crean","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Stephen Jones","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10740","person_slug":"stephen-jones","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Stephen Smith","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10594","person_slug":"stephen-smith","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Steve Georganas","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10245","person_slug":"steve-georganas","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Steve Gibbons","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10250","person_slug":"steve-gibbons","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Steve Irons","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10326","person_slug":"steve-irons","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Steven Ciobo","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10122","person_slug":"steven-ciobo","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Stuart Robert","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10545","person_slug":"stuart-robert","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Burke","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10081","person_slug":"tony-burke","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Crook","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10735","person_slug":"tony-crook","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tony Windsor","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10676","person_slug":"tony-windsor","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tony Zappia","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10695","person_slug":"tony-zappia","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Warren Entsch","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10203","person_slug":"warren-entsch","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Warren Truss","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10641","person_slug":"warren-truss","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Wayne Swan","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10617","person_slug":"wayne-swan","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Wyatt Roy","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10732","person_slug":"wyatt-roy","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Yvette D'Ath","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10164","person_slug":"yvette-dath","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Mental Health - Recommital of Vote - Greens amendment","noes":3,"question":"The majority voted in favour of a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org/debates/?id=2010-11-25.45.2) that the words which Greens MP [Adam Bandt](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Adam_Bandt&mpc=Melbourne&house=representatives) wanted to omit remain unchanged. By voting 'aye' for this motion, the majority supported the wording of the [original motion](http://www.openaustralia.org/debates/?id=2010-10-25.184.1) and rejected Mr Bandt's [amendment](http://www.openaustralia.org/debate/?id=2010-11-25.28.1) to it. Mr Bandt's amendment was to Liberal MP [Peter Dutton](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Peter_Dutton&mpc=Dickson&house=representatives)'s original motion:(Read Mr Bandt's full explanation of his amendment [here](http://www.openaustralia.org/debate/?id=2010-11-25.28.1). ) _That paragraph 2 be omitted with a view to substituting the following words:_ _“(2) requires the Government to:_ _(a) expand ongoing primary health care programmes to target those in need, the vulnerable and long-term clientele working with the community and NGO sector;_ _(b) provide alternatives to emergency department treatment such as multi-disciplinary community-based sub-acute services that supports ‘stepped’ (two-staged) prevention and recovery care;_ _(c) establish a national network of one-stop shop community mental health centres;_ _(d) provide additional training for GPs and nurses to triage mental health;_ _(e) expand the number of headspace centres to a minimum of 90 nationally;_ _(f) establish a national network of 20 EPPIC centres;_ _(g) provide an additional 800 beds for mental health, associated with the EPPIC centres;_ _(h) appropriate funds necessary to provide these critical steps to expanding mental health treatment facilities; and_ _(i) immediately provide additional funds for existing headspace centres, respite treatment and primary health care programmes; and”_ One member, Nationals MP [Tony Crook](http://publi","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-representatives-798","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/representatives/2010-11-25/3"}
